<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilbert Elliot, 1st Earl of Minto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1751">1751</a>–<a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sir Gilbert Elliot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> Elliot, 1st Earl of Minto, was a Scottish politician and diplomat. He served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of the Anglo-Corsican Kingdom from 1794 to 1796, governing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bastia">Bastia</a> under a British-backed constitution, until the British evacuated the island. He was later governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1807 to 1813.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilbert-elliot-1st-earl-of-minto.jpg" alt="Gilbert Elliot, 1st Earl of Minto" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Atkinson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gilbert_Eliot,_1st_Earl_of_Minto_by_James_Atkinson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
